00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.490
I think the thing that
I wanna start off with

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:13.490
this afternoon, this evening,
is putting into context

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.100
something that's been running
through my mind a lot lately

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.920
which is perspective.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.840
What's really fascinating
to me is something

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.290
that's emerged as almost
difficult to fully understand

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.540
which is it's unbelievable
that life is as basic

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.590
as how do you see it.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.950
For me, I've been saying a lot lately

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.360
and have always and to a
lot of people close to me

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.880
a statement that says you
find what you're looking for.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.680
If you're looking for negativity,
it's very easy to find.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.210
If you're looking for positivity,
it's very easy to find.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.310
If you think it's going to be successful,

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.190
you start to see signals
that lead to that.

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:57.530
And if you think it's gonna
fail, you'll see that.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.900
If you're cynical and a
pessimist, that's what you see.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.470
If you're optimistic and positive,

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.520
that's what you're gonna see.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.790
And really, the vulnerability

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:12.430
to the way I roll, which is
optimistic and positivity,

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.650
is you could become delusional.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.260
It's not practical.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.460
You think you can just
dream it into success.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.490
You don't understand the requirements

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.480
and the costs and the sacrifices

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.810
that are needed to actually get somewhere.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.140
I think the biggest thing

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.660
that I've been spending time on lately

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.430
from a perspective standpoint
is we are all now affected

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.430
by the last 10 to 15
years of entrepreneurship

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.750
and when we look at stories like Facebook

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.380
or WeChat or Uber or Weibo,

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.770
we see these extreme monstrous successes

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:52.400
and they cloud the fact
that for the 15 companies

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.210
that actually got to billions in revenue

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.500
and actually run actual businesses

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.510
not predicated on venture capital,

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.730
there's 80 trillion
businesses that didn't.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.540
We spend all our time fascinated
on these enormous victories

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.370
without spending our time on practicality.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.490
And so, for me, what I
really wanted to establish

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.870
in this talk today is a couple things.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:21.360
One, the macro-perspective
I believe that I'm seeing

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.900
in people that are succeeding.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.900
And when I say succeeding,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.560
I think an important part of perspective

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.100
in today's day and age

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.570
is I believe that the
way we define success

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.780
is fundamentally broken in human society.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.573
We are spending way too much money,

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.740
way too much time on
putting money on a pedestal

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.540
and way little amount of time and energy

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.930
into putting happiness on a pedestal.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:53.080
The amount of millionaires,
people that make millions,

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:56.020
10 millions, hundreds of
millions of dollars a year

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.980
that I know that are
disproportionately unhappy

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.600
is staggering.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.780
And I really, really, really am passionate

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.580
about getting a conversation
into the ecosystem

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.873
of, like, why are you here?

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.700
Why are you actually here today?

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.753
What are you trying to accomplish?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.670
Do you have enough self-awareness

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.610
and understanding about yourself

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.220
to know what you're trying to achieve?

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.290
Because I promise you,
over this last decade,

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:32.800
interacting with people at
scale, publicly and privately,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.680
what's very obvious to me

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.460
is that an enormous amount of people

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.430
are trying to get success

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.330
to put make-up around
their actual insecurities.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.000
They're spending all their
time trying to make money

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.870
to hide what's actually happening.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.550
They're trying to prove
something to somebody else,

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.500
not to themselves.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.220
And no level of you finding
a path to making money

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.550
is going to solve that issue.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.400
And so, I think that we're living

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.100
through a very, very
remarkable time in our society

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.730
where this device

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:16.540
can really be an unlock to
an enormous amount of things

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.640
but I don't think people actually
know where they're going.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.870
And that's something that I've become

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.710
unbelievably fascinated with.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.150
One of the biggest
reasons I've found myself

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.020
talking more about mindset and perspective

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.550
and things of that nature

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.850
was I spend every day putting out content

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.850
that shows people exactly what to do

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.840
with their personal
brand or their business

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.470
to be successful,

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:44.990
and yet people don't take advantage

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.780
of the current state of the internet

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.723
to achieve their business goals.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.787
After a while, I started
to have to ask myself,

00:05:52.787 --> 00:05:55.070
"Why are people not doing that?"

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.990
And I didn't go into the lazy talk

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.750
of thinking people are lazy
or things of that nature.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.930
It all led to one big game of insecurity.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.870
The reason a lot of people here
don't post every single day

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.780
is 'cause they're worried
about the judgment

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.853
in the comments section of what they post.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.340
And so, before I get into the details

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.290
of what I wanna talk to you about

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.340
from a YouTube or a Facebook or a Twitter

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:27.200
or a podcast or running
ads, before any of that,

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.563
I can give you every single
tactic that is underpriced.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:36.070
But if you don't have a
foundational understanding

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:39.290
of what you like to do and why,

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.240
it's impossible for you to be successful

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.790
because we now live in a world

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:48.230
where somebody will outwork you

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.820
and take your piece.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.520
There's abundance and
there's plenty for everybody

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.420
but what has become very clear to me

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.700
is nobody beats the person

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.570
that loves what they're
doing and is good at it

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.450
because they're just always doing it.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.310
What became obvious to
me about entrepreneurship

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:13.570
is I always did it even
when it wasn't cool

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.620
or in the air like it is now.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.550
What's obvious to me today
is there are so many people

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.890
that want to be entrepreneurs
'cause it is cool today

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.150
and it's actually not who they should be.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.810
The amount of people in
this attendance today

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:31.570
who want to be entrepreneurs
or start companies

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:34.260
who would be far more
successful financially

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.480
and happy being the
number four in a company

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.253
run by an actual
entrepreneur is staggering.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.060
That's not something that anybody in here

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.700
who's delusional wants to hear.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.350
But it is still absolutely the truth.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.970
Because anytime a pendulum swings,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.710
it swings too far the other way.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:57.010
Only 15 years ago, not going to college

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.080
was not even in the cards,

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:02.560
especially not in
(chuckling) Southeast Asia.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.790
And yet now, people are debating that

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.910
and aspiring to that at scale

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:11.380
even if it has nothing to do
with who they actually are.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.020
They've just created the perception

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.750
that starting your own company
and being an entrepreneur

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:19.250
is the right or cool
or awesome thing to do.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:24.030
The only reason you should
be at this conference at all

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:28.230
is for you to find a path
to being content and happy,

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:32.040
not to make an arbitrary amount of money.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.040
I wanna make a million,
I wanna make 10 million,

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:36.030
I wanna make, arbitrary.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.350
You're just picking a fucking
number out of your ass.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.530
What you need to be doing, thanks, Mom,

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.930
what you need to be doing,
(audience chuckling)

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.510
what you need to be doing is deploying

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.983
the greatest game of self-awareness
anybody has ever done.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:54.790
This is one big game of self-awareness.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.663
I don't want you to do what I do.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.350
I was a five, six, seven,
eight, nine, 10-year-old child

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:06.350
who'd rather go and shovel
snow and wash people's car

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:10.440
and sell lemonade than
go outside and play.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.340
I was a kid who never
opened up a single textbook

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.520
from fourth grade until 12th grade.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.600
That is not necessarily who you are.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.570
And so, I start this conversation,

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:26.480
you know, (chuckling) I
flew a long way to come here

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.760
to create a very important conversation,

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.240
far more important than me telling you

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:35.650
that Instagram ads and
Stories are so underpriced

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.470
in all of Southeast Asia

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.000
that if you start buying
ads on Instagram stories

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.260
for $2 and $3 a CPM swipe-up ads

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:49.123
to a direct link to whatever
you do, whatever you sell,

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.490
as important as that tactic is,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.970
as important as it would be

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.230
for all of you to leave this conference,

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:00.180
go home, google how do I write,

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.423
how do I run Instagram Story Ads,

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.630
as much as it would
matter for me to tell you

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.580
that if you target a
certain group of people

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.060
then make the content for that group

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.660
then run $50 worth of ads

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.400
then look at the quant data then adjust it

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.970
and keep adjusting until
your cost of acquisition

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.500
is worth your lifetime value,

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.370
as important as that is,

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:31.300
as basic, as basic as
that is and important

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.550
and would work for 75% of this audience

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.513
to achieve whatever you want,

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.850
that tactic is bullshit

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:44.240
if the only thing you're
trying to do is make money.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.730
'Cause it is not sustainable.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.170
And so, look.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:53.160
I'm really, really hopeful
that my opening 10 minutes here

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:56.210
sets the tone to what
I'm trying to achieve

00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:00.370
which is, as I continue to evolve

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.700
and travel and do all this stuff,

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.840
the same themes are coming
up over and over and over.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.640
I wanna remind everybody here,

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.000
we've lived through a decade now

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.990
of economic growth and
prosperity across the world.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.960
We are in a bubble.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.950
There's so much money and
opportunity in the system

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.400
that this is not sustainable.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.960
There will be a day of reckoning

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.200
just like there was in 2007-8,

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.330
just like there was one in 2001 and '95.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.800
And for people that have lived
through some down cycles,

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.520
you think it's hard now.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:39.570
When all the money dries
up, it gets real hard.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:41.700
Let me say it very basically.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.540
If you don't have a
successful company right now

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.510
and you've been operating
for the last two years,

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:48.603
you suck.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:51.330
And I mean that.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.490
And I'm not saying that,
I'm not trying to razz,

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.320
I'm not trying to come hard.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.370
I need you to understand.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.060
How many people here run a company

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.270
or an entrepreneur start-up?

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.370
Just raise your hands.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:02.203
Raise it high.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.150
I need you to understand

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:09.140
if you're running a company
right now in the globe,

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.920
this is the easiest time
in the history of humans

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:13.833
to run a company.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.063
So, if you're not doing well,

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.533
you need to really recognize that.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.630
(chuckling) You do.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:28.080
And so, I'm unbelievably optimistic

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.230
because this thing is that special.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:34.100
I'm this optimistic

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:37.350
because the little
piece of business advice

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:41.010
in practical terms that I
slipped in five minutes ago,

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.170
I'm gonna say it one
more time nice and slow,

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:48.170
it will legitimately work
for 80% of this audience.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:53.710
Instagram Story Ads in
all of Southeast Asia,

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.560
except in Japan and China

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.240
where other platforms
dominate, not Instagram,

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:02.040
will work for your business.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:03.810
But what you have to figure out

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:07.540
is your targeting and your creative.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:10.500
The biggest reason people don't succeed

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.820
in running ads on social
networks and platforms

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.013
is 'cause they don't make enough content.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:18.600
And they don't make the content

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.640
for the audience they're trying to reach.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:24.570
They make one piece of content
and try to reach everybody.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:28.333
Contextual creative at scale is the game.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.020
It's really interesting.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.310
I've been really watching
a lot of businesses

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:42.330
and entrepreneurs navigate
the last year or so

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.350
and what's really become interesting to me

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:48.480
is the themes that play over
and over and over again.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.930
In its most basic, the biggest thing

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.400
that everybody has to leave here with

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:53.880
is the following thing.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.940
The only thing that you
should spend all your time on

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.660
to really disproportionately
grow your business

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.480
is to figure out where the customer

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.463
that you're trying to reach
spends all of their time.

