don't believe in what you're doing.

01:00:53.270 --> 01:00:56.170
But it makes it so much more
exciting when you achieve it

01:00:56.170 --> 01:00:58.089
because then you get to stick it to them.

01:00:58.089 --> 01:00:59.090
(audience chuckling)

01:00:59.090 --> 01:01:00.980
- [Harut] Well, I've never
really thought it that way but--

01:01:00.980 --> 01:01:01.813
- Well, this is the way
(audience laughing)

01:01:01.813 --> 01:01:02.646
to think about it.

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:04.620
- [Harut] Okay, uh...

01:01:04.620 --> 01:01:06.170
- But you have to understand.

01:01:06.170 --> 01:01:08.180
Nobody understands an entrepreneur

01:01:08.180 --> 01:01:10.830
if they're not an entrepreneur
'cause they want safe.

01:01:11.690 --> 01:01:13.740
But for you, you'd be unhappy being safe.

01:01:13.740 --> 01:01:15.170
You just lived it.
- Yes.

01:01:15.170 --> 01:01:17.800
- So, I have empathy for her.

01:01:17.800 --> 01:01:21.440
But you're not capable of
living your life any other way.

01:01:21.440 --> 01:01:23.560
So, here's the best part of the argument,

01:01:23.560 --> 01:01:25.470
the debate, the issue.

01:01:25.470 --> 01:01:28.040
Somebody's gonna be right.

01:01:28.040 --> 01:01:29.460
- Yes.
- Either you're gonna go

01:01:29.460 --> 01:01:33.970
and execute and provide for
your family as an entrepreneur

01:01:33.970 --> 01:01:37.290
and then you get to say to her, "See?"

01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:41.210
Or you're gonna fail and not provide

01:01:41.210 --> 01:01:42.730
and have to go get a job

01:01:42.730 --> 01:01:44.939
and then she gets to say, "See."

01:01:44.939 --> 01:01:47.240
(audience laughing)

01:01:47.240 --> 01:01:49.750
- Right, when you put it--
- That's the only two options.

01:01:49.750 --> 01:01:52.480
Either your parents are
right or you're right.

01:01:52.480 --> 01:01:54.980
Either your husband is
right or you're right.

01:01:54.980 --> 01:01:57.600
Either the commenters in
your section are right

01:01:57.600 --> 01:01:58.630
or you're right.

01:01:58.630 --> 01:02:03.540
I spend no time on the
cheering or the boos.

01:02:03.540 --> 01:02:08.120
I spend on executing so
that when it goes to 000,

01:02:08.120 --> 01:02:09.723
I can say I was right.

01:02:10.686 --> 01:02:13.580
- (hoots) Yes!
(audience applauding)

01:02:13.580 --> 01:02:15.930
- And just slightly adding on to that,

01:02:15.930 --> 01:02:18.020
I know you've had previous videos

01:02:18.020 --> 01:02:21.690
where you talked about
handling hate on social media,

01:02:21.690 --> 01:02:24.480
kind of acknowledge them and
you start a conversation,

01:02:24.480 --> 01:02:25.550
bring the
- I think, yeah, keep going.

01:02:25.550 --> 01:02:26.830
- positivity into it.

01:02:26.830 --> 01:02:30.180
But how do you, like, do you
address every one of them?

01:02:30.180 --> 01:02:32.380
Because at end of the day,
it still takes up your time.

01:02:32.380 --> 01:02:35.263
- Yeah, I can't address
all of my hate anymore.

01:02:35.263 --> 01:02:37.270
(audience chuckling)

01:02:37.270 --> 01:02:40.420
But I think that too many people,

01:02:40.420 --> 01:02:43.130
when somebody says something
they don't like to hear,

01:02:43.130 --> 01:02:46.120
dismiss it as hate and a troll.

01:02:46.120 --> 01:02:48.840
I read it and question it

01:02:48.840 --> 01:02:51.180
and then decide is there any merit to it.

01:02:51.180 --> 01:02:53.370
And the reason I've been able to evolve

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:54.970
is because I don't just default

01:02:54.970 --> 01:02:57.400
if somebody disagrees
with me or makes fun of me

01:02:57.400 --> 01:02:58.400
that they're wrong.

01:02:58.400 --> 01:03:01.010
I try to be thoughtful
about what are they doing.

01:03:01.010 --> 01:03:04.010
Nine out of 10 times, it's
'cause they're in a bad place

01:03:04.010 --> 01:03:05.910
and they're just trying to drag me down.

01:03:05.910 --> 01:03:07.820
But occasionally, there's a point there

01:03:07.820 --> 01:03:09.200
that I kind of fester in

01:03:09.200 --> 01:03:12.150
and start subconsciously
adjusting what I'm doing.

01:03:12.150 --> 01:03:14.230
Feedback is important.

01:03:14.230 --> 01:03:16.113
- Perfect, thank you.
- You're welcome.

01:03:16.113 --> 01:03:18.150
(audience applauding)

01:03:18.150 --> 01:03:19.210
- [Reagan] Hi, Gary.

01:03:19.210 --> 01:03:20.560
- One more?

01:03:20.560 --> 01:03:22.380
Guys, I only have time
for one more question.

01:03:22.380 --> 01:03:23.830
I apologize.
- Hi, Gary.

01:03:23.830 --> 01:03:24.880
My name is Reagan.

01:03:24.880 --> 01:03:26.420
Basically, I wanna ask, as an entrepreneur

01:03:26.420 --> 01:03:27.870
where you're hustling every single day,

01:03:27.870 --> 01:03:29.490
- Yes.
- and sometimes, you know,

01:03:29.490 --> 01:03:30.560
