01:07:04.920 --> 01:07:06.070
- [Gary] Thank you.

01:07:06.070 --> 01:07:08.190
- But also, you know, I
wanted to bring to a point.

01:07:08.190 --> 01:07:10.600
How do you, you talked about framing

01:07:10.600 --> 01:07:12.810
contextual creative at scale.

01:07:12.810 --> 01:07:15.600
- Yes.
- How do you do that,

01:07:15.600 --> 01:07:17.040
or do you have a structure?

01:07:17.040 --> 01:07:18.470
How do you frame it?

01:07:18.470 --> 01:07:20.500
I understand, you also
mentioned to one of the ladies,

01:07:20.500 --> 01:07:22.880
Marie or something,

01:07:22.880 --> 01:07:26.020
that Q and A is one of
the innovative ways,

01:07:26.020 --> 01:07:26.853
but what are the other ways,

01:07:26.853 --> 01:07:29.520
aside from the three
different types of media?

01:07:29.520 --> 01:07:32.980
- What I mean by that in
its most important form

01:07:32.980 --> 01:07:35.340
is when you're talking to somebody,

01:07:35.340 --> 01:07:37.690
you need to relate to them.

01:07:37.690 --> 01:07:39.820
So, if you're making a piece of content

01:07:39.820 --> 01:07:41.960
to 18- to 20-year-olds,
- I'm the crazy guy that...

01:07:41.960 --> 01:07:45.540
- you need to use adjectives
and cultural references

01:07:45.540 --> 01:07:47.310
to an 18- to 20-year-old.

01:07:47.310 --> 01:07:49.524
- Does that include cursing?
- You know what I mean?

01:07:49.524 --> 01:07:51.390
I mean, that's the point.

01:07:51.390 --> 01:07:53.850
The point is you need to make
it contextual to the audience.

01:07:53.850 --> 01:07:55.710
When I speak here,

01:07:55.710 --> 01:07:57.680
there's a lot of things
that I didn't say today

01:07:57.680 --> 01:07:59.930
that I would've definitely
said if I was in New York

01:07:59.930 --> 01:08:01.780
because it would've made
sense to New Yorkers

01:08:01.780 --> 01:08:03.480
but wouldn't have made sense here.

01:08:04.800 --> 01:08:08.660
On YouTube, I can make a 41-minute video.

01:08:08.660 --> 01:08:10.210
On Instagram, it was a minute.

01:08:10.210 --> 01:08:13.190
Then IGTV came, and now it can be 41.

01:08:13.190 --> 01:08:15.490
So, you have to respect the platform

01:08:15.490 --> 01:08:18.480
but first you have to respect
who you're trying to reach.

01:08:18.480 --> 01:08:20.460
- Okay.
- So, when I say contextual

01:08:20.460 --> 01:08:24.040
at scale, it's what audience
are you trying to reach

01:08:24.040 --> 01:08:27.850
and then do you use what
slang, what references.

01:08:27.850 --> 01:08:28.960
Do you understand?
- Yeah.

01:08:28.960 --> 01:08:31.550
- Too many people are
trying to reach everybody.

01:08:31.550 --> 01:08:34.370
Which means you're not reaching anybody.

01:08:34.370 --> 01:08:36.010
It's vanilla.

01:08:36.010 --> 01:08:37.080
You understand?

01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:40.810
So, again, this is the theme of this talk.

01:08:40.810 --> 01:08:42.890
When you make so much content,

01:08:42.890 --> 01:08:45.267
when I make a video that says,

01:08:45.267 --> 01:08:48.377
"50 years," "for the next
50 years," "50-year-olds,"

01:08:48.377 --> 01:08:50.170
"you've got 50 more years to live,"

01:08:50.170 --> 01:08:52.337
